Road Relocation
July7,2021
ROAD DESIGN
Theroadwas designed to incorporate the General Site Requirements(ATS, Date Unknown)provided as
following design elements were incorporated intotheroad design:
·The roadway is16-feetwideand 23-feetwide through90-degree horizontal curves
The inside edge of travelway through90-degree horizontal curves has a minimum radius of
135-feet
Vertical curves will not exceed6-inches of elevation difference over50-feet
Topsoil willbe stripped to a depthof 4-inches and will be replaced after completion of roadway
native ground elevations and promote drainage
Theroadway design matches existing ground elevations as closely as possible while meeting the
minimum design requirements to provide sheet flow across the roadway
Native subgrade will be moisture conditioned and compacted to a thickness of one foot.The
specified density and moisture content is95%of themaximum dry density andplus orminus3%
of the optimum moisture content perASTM D698.The subgrade will be proof-rolled prior to
placing the geo textile fabric
A 10-ounce woven geo textile fabric will be placed beneath the gravel surfacing
The gravel surfacingis8-inches thick.The specified density and moisture content is98%of the
maximum dry density and plus or minus2%of the optimum moisture content perAST MD698
The construction specifications areprovided in the Construction Drawings provided as Attachment C.
